<file path="docs/specs/solidity/cbor-metadata/plan.md">
# Implementation plan

1. Use cborg 6.1.3 (Apache-2.0) as a pinned format decoder, with a bounded
   tokenizer at its owning adapter boundary. Decode maps as Map, preserve integer
   precision and strictly validate emitted text bytes before conversion.
2. Add the portable metadata-result schema in src/domain/evm/. Use exact byte
   ranges into the already retained bytecode rather than copying an opaque CBOR
   hex payload into every selected summary.
3. Add src/evm/SolidityMetadata.ts to interpret the terminal length/root-map
   candidate. Return unavailable, decoded, partial or not-decoded facts; keep
   unsupported nested values explicit instead of recursively expanding them.
4. Compute the facts in EvmoleInterfaceWorker from its selected bytes. The host
   provider validates ranges/identity and projects the additive metadata field.
   Preserve raw engine output without rewriting its unknown-precision metadata.
5. Ensure the canonical EVM bytecode shape carries the optional field into complete
   and summary Evidence. Include decoding profile, coverage and limitations.
6. Add producer, worker, historical contract and public MCP boundary coverage.
   Compile an owned Solidity fixture with a pinned caller-supplied solc module,
   and verify its CBOR compiler version. Run relevant static/architecture checks.
7. Extend the existing real Linux CLI/MCP verifier with independent metadata
   assertions. Run the compiler-setting matrix in its CI lane and classify its
   verifier as EVM-owned, with a production CI-planner regression.

No new execution provider or target authority is introduced: a format parser is
added inside the existing EVM worker. Linux x64 provider admission, target-free
semantics, cleanup, limits and complete original Evidence remain unchanged.
No metadata JSON or source URL is automatically acquired.

The parser bounds nesting to 64 and token/collection growth to the selected
terminal payload's byte count (the format's terminal length is at most 65535).
Every data item consumes encoded bytes; broad declared collection lengths cannot
justify allocation without that lower bound. Expanded results still pass the
worker's existing 16 MiB output check.
</file>

<file path="docs/specs/solidity/cbor-metadata/spec.md">
# Solidity terminal metadata inspection

Issue: https://github.com/morluto/rea/issues/2388

## Outcome

The existing EVM interface operation should retain independently decoded terminal
CBOR candidate facts from the exact selected bytes instead of relying on precision
unknowns in the engine's reported metadata. This increment covers trailer ranges,
bounded decoding, exact integer/non-text scalar key evidence and compiler-version
representations.

## Requirements

- Preserve the existing carrier/decoded identities and original full bytecode.
- Report a plausible terminal root-map candidate separately from proof of Solidity
  origin. Missing or non-map trailers remain unavailable, not proven absent.
- Interpret scalar root-map keys/values losslessly: integers as decimal strings,
  bytes as hex, strings, booleans and null. Preserve undecoded/unsupported values
  through the original bytecode plus exact candidate offset/length.
- Report partial and not-decoded coverage, parser/profile failures and unsupported
  CBOR forms explicitly. Do not silently coerce unknown keys into object properties.
- Interpret admitted solc release/prerelease representations only from observed
  entries; preserve ambiguity if duplicate compiler-version keys occur.
- Keep the additive field compatible with historical Evidence and retain
  it through selected summary delivery and public CLI/MCP.
  Historical omission parses as a null unknown facet without mutating the source.
- Bound nesting before decoder recursion and collection lengths before allocation.
  Keep parsing inside the existing owned worker and its resource/output budgets.
- Do not fetch metadata or source content, contact RPC or execute contract code.

## Acceptance and limits

Owned compiler fixtures and malformed/synthetic trailers cover integers beyond
Number precision, non-text keys, nested/uninterpreted values, invalid UTF-8,
invalid lengths, unsupported tags and nesting bounds. Public boundary tests
preserve the field and older omission. A real pinned solc artifact verifies actual
metadata facts; the existing Linux-only EVM host profile remains unchanged.

## Deferred issue criteria

Binding a supplied metadata JSON to IPFS/Swarm commitments is a later independent
increment of #2388. This PR must reference rather than close the whole issue.
</file>

